Changes made by DMD61 to the original HDRDisplayCalibrate code:
- Guided sensor dialogs in the HDR wizard and in Verify & report.
- The ArgyllCMS bundled next to the exe is always used first; the bin folder is read-only when it is bundled.
- Italian translation of the interface.
- HDR wizard: opens on HDR or SDR calibration according to the monitor and switches Windows HDR on/off by itself;
  "Before you start" box; numbered steps in the profile prompt; final profile name; closing window; report export to
  PDF or HTML saved automatically; HDR colour check (24 colours, dE2000); work folder emptied at the end.
- Version 0.1.0 of DMD TV Calibrate: new program name, executable (DMDTVCalibrate.exe), icon, and its own settings
  and documents folders (DMDTVCalibrate), so it can be installed side by side with HDRDisplayCalibrate.
- The monitor calibration pages (SDR and HDR calibration, verify, gamut, 3D LUT, profiles) and the sign-in LUT
  loader were removed: DMD TV Calibrate is for TVs only. The log page moved to its own file.
- TV calibration page (version 0.1.0, step 1): TV model list with an "Other TV (generic)" mode for any brand,
  video / PC levels, measurement window, target gamma and white, probe placement guide for TVs (contact with the
  counterweight or tripod), full-screen TV patch window with aiming mark, initial measurement of grey scale and
  colours against Rec.709 / D65 with charts, CSV and PDF / HTML report. Monitor-only rows (ACM, DDC/CI, ICC / MHC2
  profiles) were removed from the Display & sensor page.
- Guided steps 4 (white luminance) and 5 (2-point white balance: gain and offset) with continuous readings, suggested
  menu values and learning of the size of one menu step; the live meter page rewritten for the TV patch window
  (monitor functions DDC/CI auto OSD and room light removed); the display calibration curve is set to linear while
  measuring and restored afterwards.
